    {
      "claim_id": "majority-ground",
      "proposition": "The Court holds that Kisor v. Wilkie, 588 U.S. 558 (2019), modified Stinson v. United States, 508 U.S. 36 (1993), because Stinson explicitly grounded deference to Sentencing Guidelines commentary on Bowles v. Seminole Rock & Sand Co., 325 U.S. 410 (1945), so courts may defer to Guidelines commentary only if the Guideline text remains genuinely ambiguous after exhausting all traditional tools of statutory construction."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "ground-breadth",
      "proposition": "The Court announces a categorical methodological rule governing all official commentary to the United States Sentencing Guidelines across all federal criminal sentencings, while declining to resolve in the first instance whether U.S.S.G. \u00a7 2K2.1(a)(3)'s 'large capacity magazine' provision is genuinely ambiguous as applied to petitioner's 17-round magazine, remanding that question to the Fifth Circuit."
    }
  ],
